 Sieyès asked what the Third Estate was, and what it asked. This essay ends by asking the same of the record it has described. What is the chain? A register. What has it been until now in the political order? Nothing — a curiosity, an asset class, a subject of regulation. What can it become? A constitution: the first one that no party wrote, that binds the strong before they are strong, that cannot see what its subjects are, and under which the estate that does everything is already something.
 
